# WO-L4 The site looks real

## Goal

Standing on the road in `Play.unity`, the headset player sees a construction site, not a drawing: textured ground with relief, a real trench with spoil, bedding and pipe, a gravel road, fences, cones and barriers, the trailer, the crews and machines, a sky with sun and clouds, shadows, and haze toward the horizon, inside the Quest 3S budget of `Docs/XR_RENDERING.md`. Every site material uses one shader, `LOBOver/SiteLit`, so WO-L5 can add the warp to all of them at once. Bryan's words on the first build: the assets are extremely poor, it does not feel realistic, a horizontal line like a drawing.

## Read

- `AGENTS.md`, `Docs/XR_RENDERING.md` (all of it), `Docs/LEVEL1.md` ("In the headset"), `Docs/DECISIONS.md` K37 to K40
- `Assets/LOBOver/Editor/{PlaySceneBuilder,SiteAssetBuilder,SiteSceneBuilder,BuildingBlocksSetup}.cs`, `Assets/LOBOver/Runtime/World/**` (StationCell, CrewRig, SiteWorld, WorldAssets, WorldDrawing), `Assets/LOBOver/Runtime/Play/HostWorldPresenter.cs`, `Assets/LOBOver/Art/PlaySky.shader`, `Tools/import_lobgame_assets.ps1`
- LOB-Game's assets already imported under `Assets/LOBGame/` (the sand pile photoscan with its textures, `pipe/` with PBR textures, `road-barrier-collection`, `trafic-cone`, `water-barriers`, `Construction Assets/Traffic Props` fences and jersey barrier, the workers and machines) and the ones this order adds: `3D_Models/Tree` (`Tree 2/fast-urban-tree`, `Tree 2/beech`, `Tree1/tree`), `3D_Models/sophiaImports` (`trench_DigNFill_03.fbx` with its `groundTrenchDig` albedo, normal and metallic-smoothness textures), `3D_Models/traffic-props`, `3D_Models/construction-site-barrier`
- `Assets/Settings/Mobile_RPAsset.asset`, `Mobile_Renderer.asset`, `Assets/Oculus/OculusProjectConfig.asset`

## You may change

`Assets/LOBOver/Editor/**`, `Assets/LOBOver/Runtime/**`, `Assets/LOBOver/Art/**` (including generated textures and materials), `Assets/LOBOver/Tests/**`, `Assets/Settings/Mobile_RPAsset.asset` and `Mobile_Renderer.asset` (only the values named below), `Tools/import_lobgame_assets.ps1` (add folders only), `Play.unity` only through the builder. Never `Assets/LOBGame/**` (copies go to `Assets/LOBOver/Art/Converted/` as now), never a `[BuildingBlock]` object.

## Build

1. **Imports.** Add the four LOB-Game folders above to `Tools/import_lobgame_assets.ps1`; the orchestrator runs it before verification. Convert their Built-in materials to URP copies the way `SiteAssetBuilder` already does; every converted material ends on `LOBOver/SiteLit` (item 2) with its textures kept.
2. **`LOBOver/SiteLit`** (URP HLSL, `Art/SiteLit.shader`): opaque, lit through `UniversalFragmentPBR` with the main light and its shadows, SH ambient, fog; base map, normal map, smoothness and occlusion (a metallic-smoothness map where the source has one); tiling in world units for ground materials (triplanar for the ground mesh, so no stretching on slopes); a `_Splat` keyword variant for the ground that blends three tiled layers (dirt, gravel, dry grass) by vertex colour r, g, b; GPU instancing; the stereo macros of `XR_RENDERING.md`. One material per surface kind under `Art/Materials/`. The old `Soil`, `AccessRoad`, `Timber`, `StorageSteel`, `Repair_SiteCabin` copies move to this shader with the textures below.
3. **Textures.** If `Assets/` holds `TerrainLayer` assets or tileable textures whose names contain grass, dirt, soil, mud or gravel (a pack Bryan imported), use the best three for the ground layers and a dirt one for the trench. Otherwise generate them: an Editor generator writes tileable 1024Â² albedo, normal and smoothness textures to `Art/Generated/` for packed dirt (fBm with fine grain), gravel (Worley cells with varied stone tint), dry grass (streaked fBm, straw and olive), and a 256Â² soft dust sprite (radial falloff, brown, alpha) for the work particles. Normal maps from the height field; `sRGB` on albedo only; ASTC 6x6 on Android. LOB-Game's `groundTrenchDig` textures are the trench wall and bedding; the sand pile's albedo and occlusion are the spoil.
4. **Ground.** Replace the flat bank boxes with a built mesh, 1,200 m by 200 m, 2 m cells within 30 m of the trench and 10 m cells beyond (under 60,000 triangles), with gentle relief (fBm, 0.6 m amplitude, flat within 8 m of the trench and the road), vertex colours painting gravel on the road and its shoulders, dirt within 12 m of the trench, dry grass beyond, with noisy edges. A gravel road 4 m wide along the trench at `WorldUnits.RoadZ` with two shallow ruts. Beyond 100 m from the trench the ground continues as a simple plane to 3,000 m so the horizon never ends in a line against the sky. No colliders are needed on the site in Level 1 (the hub floor collider stays).
5. **Trench.** Per station cell, real geometry: a 1.2 m wide, 1.8 m deep cut with slightly irregular walls (noise-displaced), the trench wall texture; bedding gravel in the bottom when piped; LOB-Game's `PIPE.fbx` with its PBR textures as the laid pipe; a continuous spoil windrow on the far side from the road (noise-displaced mounds with the spoil texture, 1 m high, breaking every 30 m), the photoscanned sand pile as a hero pile at each crew's station; the slumped wall as a collapsed wedge with loose material on the floor; standing water as a dark reflective plane 0.3 m above the floor; seepage as a dark wet band on the lower wall; backfilled cells as a disturbed dirt strip at grade. Stakes: wooden lath 1.2 m, 5 cm wide, pink flagging, and a small station sign with the station text in 4 cm letters readable from the road.
6. **Props and surroundings.** Fences (`fence_long`) along the road's outer edge every 10 m for 60 m either side of each crew; cones and a barrier at the collapse and around each working machine; two jersey barriers at the gate; the trailer as a box with the site cabin material, a door and a window; a tree line (the lightest LOB-Game tree under 8,000 triangles, at most 30 instances, GPU instanced) 80 to 120 m beyond the far side with gaps; nothing within 20 m of the player that is a bare box.
7. **Sky and light.** A dome shader `LOBOver/SiteSky` (replaces `PlaySky`): if a cubemap skybox material exists under `Assets/` use its cubemap, else a procedural sky (zenith to horizon gradient, sun disc at the light's direction with a soft halo, two fBm cloud layers drifting slowly, a haze band at the horizon). The directional light: elevation 48Â°, warm white, soft shadows, one cascade, 2048, 60 m. Ambient trilight tuned to the sky. Linear fog 300 to 2,500 m in the horizon colour. Rain and the cloud bank keep working through `SiteSky`.
8. **Particles.** The work particles use the dust sprite on URP Particles/Unlit (alpha blended, soft, brown, small); no untextured white sprites anywhere.
9. **Settings** (values only): Mobile RP asset render scale 1.0, MSAA 4x, HDR off, no post-processing; `XRRuntimeSettings` foveation Low; static batching on the builder's static geometry; GPU instancing on repeated props.
10. **Scale sanity.** A worker is 1.8 m, the excavator cab roof about 3.2 m, the pipe 0.3 m outside diameter, the trench 1.2 m wide; the builder logs any imported model whose bounds are off by more than 25% and scales it.
11. **Tests.** EditMode: the builder runs twice and changes nothing the second time; every renderer under `[LOBOver] Site` uses `LOBOver/SiteLit`, `LOBOver/SiteSky` or URP Particles/Unlit; no material has a null main texture except the sky; the Editor stats at the pipe crew's station facing across the trench stay under 300k triangles and 150 draw calls (read through `UnityEditor.UnityStats`); the generated textures are tileable (the left and right edge columns match within 2%).

## Acceptance checks

- Orchestrator through the MCP: import script run; compile clean; Play Scene twice; tests pass; Play in the Editor with `Play LOB Over.cmd` running and the game started, at the pipe crew's station at eye height: screenshots facing across the trench, along the trench toward the excavator and toward the backfill crew, and one from the road at the collapse after Day 4, all through the preview camera at 1440 by 1440. Reviewed against the goal's first sentence: textured ground with relief, trench with spoil and pipe, road, fences and props, sky with clouds, shadows, haze, no white blobs, no bare boxes near the player; stats under budget.
- No build. Bryan builds and judges in the headset (K35, K41).

## Out of scope

The warp (WO-L5), the hub panel, voices, the Plan page.

## Amendment 1 (orchestrator, 2026-10-21 12:25)

Item 7, the sky: the procedural sky is the default. A cubemap skybox found under `Assets/` is used only when the sun probed from it sits above 30 degrees of elevation; then the light is aimed at it. In every other case the directional light keeps its 48 degree elevation and the procedural sky draws the sun disc at the light's direction with the cloud layers and the haze band. Reason: round 1 aimed the light at a daytime cubemap whose sun sits on the horizon, and the whole site went dark.

## Amendment 2 (orchestrator, 2026-10-22 00:05, from Bryan's round 3 authorization)

Two presentation requirements added to items 5 and 7. Item 7, the clouds: the two cloud layers fade out completely within 8 degrees of the horizon (zero cloud at and below 8 degrees of elevation, full strength again by about 16 degrees), and the cloud projection never stretches into radial streaks near the horizon; the haze band stays. Item 5, the trench walls: every trench surface (both walls, the slumped wall, the wet lower band, the floor) is textured by triplanar mapping in world units (about 1 m per tile) so the dirt texture reads continuous with no stretching or streaks, within the three-samples-per-layer rule of `Docs/XR_RENDERING.md`.

# WO-L4 rejection 3 (2026-10-22 00:40), the final round, authorized by Bryan

Round 2 was verified as before (`Docs/WORKLOG.md`, 12:25 to 12:45): import, compile, Play Scene twice, EditMode 23/25, Play against the launcher's host on Day 8. Bryan authorized one more round for the three open items plus two presentation items he added (`WO-L4.md`, Amendment 2). Every cause below was traced in the Editor tonight; fix exactly these five, everything under "Passed" stays.

## Failed

1. **Budget.** `SitePresentationTests.PipeStationPreviewStaysInsideQuestBudget` reports no number (item 3) and my own measurement through one camera at the pipe crew's station facing across the trench, Game view maximized, read 344,420 triangles and 120 draw calls on Day 8 (240,211 on Day 9 in round 1). Expected under 300,000 and 150. Findings (`Monitor/out/unity/l4-tris.txt`, `l4-frustum.txt`):
   - In EditMode the `[BuildingBlock] Camera Rig` subtree has 228 enabled renderers sitting at the rig origin, all shadow casters: the four controller-model variants (left/right touch 58,660 and 58,564, rainier 23,324 each, oculus_controller 22,436 and 16,872 each, controller_ply 13,340 each), the hand meshes and 146 `HandSphereMap` spheres (112,128). About 394,000 shadow-pass triangles that OVR hides at runtime but the EditMode test renders. Required in the test: disable every renderer under the Camera Rig for the measured frame and restore them (they are not site content; log their count separately); one `camera.Render()` per frame; read `UnityStats` on the frame after the render; keep the camera isolation and the Game-view maximize; guard destroyed cameras (item 3).
   - `Ground` (46,322) and `Horizon` (688) cast shadows onto nothing but themselves: 47,010 shadow triangles every frame. Required: `shadowCastingMode = Off` on both (they still receive).
   - The tree line costs 6,017 triangles per tree in the main pass (Tree_0 and Tree_1 instances read 18,051 in view on Day 0, up to about 91,000 with more of the 21 instances in the frustum). Required: beyond 60 m a tree is two crossed, alpha-clipped quads (4 triangles) with an albedo and alpha baked once by the builder from the tree model (512 by 512, into `Art/Generated/`, `_ALPHATEST_ON` on `LOBOver/SiteLit`), GPU instanced, no shadows; the beech mesh stays only as the bake source.
   - Machines and workers cast shadows at any distance: the worker is 18,240 triangles, the crane 32,930, the excavator 209,448. Required: a crew's renderers cast shadows only while the crew is within 30 m of the player (CrewRig checks the distance to the rig's head about once a second and toggles `shadowCastingMode`).
   - `Play_Excavator_*.prefab` is 209,448 triangles because the WorkMotion wrapper holds a second complete copy of the machine, `Mesh1552` (120,812), beside the rigged `excavator_05_noTranslation:*` parts (88,636). Required in `SiteModelBuilder`: keep one copy (the rigged parts), and an `LODGroup` that shows the full model within 60 m and the builder's rig boxes (Body, Boom scaled to the model's bounds) beyond. Facing along the trench toward the excavator is reviewed in a screenshot and reported with its number.
   Expected after the fix: the test logs `WO-L4 preview 1440x1440: N triangles` with N under 300,000 and fewer than 150 draw calls; my Day-8 check at the pipe crew's station facing across the trench stays under 300,000.

2. **Rebuild not identical.** `PlayRebuildHasIdenticalGeometryMaterialsAndArtBytes` fails on `Art/Converted/Play_StationCell.prefab` (hash `Z/tZâ€¦` against `Bq0/â€¦`); each Play Scene re-saves the prefab with new file ids and a new object order. Traced with `SiteModelBuilder.SameContent(fresh, saved)`: it returns false because the fresh hierarchy has 152 objects and the saved prefab 151. The extra object is the `MeshFilter` that TextMeshPro adds to `StationStake/Station` with `HideFlags.HideInInspector | HideAndDontSave`; it is never serialized, so the saved prefab lacks it and the GameObject's `m_Component` array sizes differ. Required in `SiteModelBuilder.HierarchyObjects` and `SameContent`: skip components whose `hideFlags` include `DontSave`, and compare a GameObject's component list through those filtered entries rather than the raw `m_Component` array. Expected: `SameContent` true on an unchanged rebuild, no save, the second Play Scene leaves the prefab byte-identical, the test passes.

3. **Camera restore.** `PipeStationPreviewStaysInsideQuestBudget` throws `MissingReferenceException: The object of type 'UnityEngine.Camera' has been destroyed` at `SitePresentationTests.cs:242` (`entry.camera.enabled = false`): `Resources.FindObjectsOfTypeAll<Camera>()` returns cameras destroyed by earlier tests. Required: drop destroyed cameras (`c == null` in Unity's sense) when collecting `otherCameras`, and guard both loops. Expected: the test reports its number.

4. **Clouds at the horizon** (Amendment 2). `Art/SiteSky.shader`, the procedural branch: `float2 uv = d.xz / max(0.12, d.y)` with the cloud term scaled by `smoothstep(0, 0.15, d.y)` leaves the two cloud layers stretched into radial streaks down to the horizon (`Monitor/out/unity/l4c-sky.png`, and the "rain" streaks under the clouds in `l4-quad2-shot.png`). Required: multiply the cloud term by `smoothstep(0.139, 0.276, d.y)` (zero at and below 8 degrees of elevation, full by 16) and clamp the projection divisor at `max(d.y, 0.139)` so nothing stretches under the fade; the haze band and the sun stay as they are.

5. **Trench surfaces** (Amendment 2). The walls show horizontal smears and vertical bands every tile, and the shadowed far wall reads black (`l4-trench-baseline-A.png`, `l4-trench-baseline-B.png`). The cause is the texture, not the mesh or the shader: `TrenchWall`, `WetTrench` and `Bedding` tile `groundTrenchDig_model_001_standardSurface1_AlbedoTransparency.1001` (2048Â², LOB-Game's UV atlas for the `trench_DigNFill_03` model, with dilated padding and black empty regions) at 1 m through the `_WORLD` projection. A Unity Quad with `TrenchWall.mat` shows the same smears (`l4-quad2-shot.png`); the wall meshes' normals are (0, 0, Â±1) with valid tangents; shadows off and normal map off change nothing (`l4-trench-noshadow-A.png`, `l4-trench-nobump-A.png`). Required in `SiteMaterialBuilder`: the trench wall, the slumped wall, the floor and the wet band use the tileable dirt layer the ground already uses (`Muddy` base, normal and mask), tinted about (0.80, 0.75, 0.70) for the cut and (0.45, 0.42, 0.40) for the wet band; the bedding uses the tileable gravel layer; all through the existing `_WORLD` triplanar path at 1 m tiles. The `groundTrenchDig` textures are not tiled anywhere (they may stay on the `trench_DigNFill_03` model if it is placed as a UV-mapped prop). Expected: continuous dirt on both walls from the road and from the far side, no black wall in shadow; I check with the same renders.

## Passed (keep)

Everything listed under "Passed" in rejections 1 and 2, plus round 2's procedural sky with the sun at 48 degrees, the TextMeshPro station sign, the colour tolerance and the Game-view isolation.

## Scope note

`Assets/Orchestrator/` is orchestrator tooling in the working tree; ignore it in the scope check. Unity cannot be run from the sandbox; compile with `Assets/LOBOver/Tests/CompileOffline.ps1` as before.


